{"parentUuid":"062c5429-f902-4926-adb5-1b27012b0ca5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrhDkbQB2KiTMjJmUQ3c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21526,"cache_read_input_tokens":29474,"output_tokens":770,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":89},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":21526,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":770,"cache_read_input_tokens":29474,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21526,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":21526},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":444,"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfrhDkLHBub4YTtTcPKBM","type":"assistant","uuid":"b9adbe15-b41f-4eb4-8e3f-40c7d46f7ce6","timestamp":"2026-10-09T12:52:00.049Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"21836f70-90a0-4ca0-837b-2f1d58976556","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/private/tmp/hm-capture-claude","sessionId":"7d8ceea2-1c2b-4581-8f12-c261e4a673ec","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"master"}
{"parentUuid":"b9adbe15-b41f-4eb4-8e3f-40c7d46f7ce6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrhDkbQB2KiTMjJmUQ3c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**The Lantern Fox**\n\nEvery winter, when the snow lay thick over the hollow, a red fox named Ilse came down from the ridge to watch the village lights.\n\nShe was not supposed to be there. The farmers set traps along the stone wall, and the old dog at the mill barked at anything with a bushy tail. But Ilse had found a gap beneath the orchard fence, and from the frozen ditch she could see the window of a small house where a girl named Maren sat each night, drawing pictures by lamplight.\n\nMaren drew animals. Owls, badgers, a stag with antlers like tangled branches. Ilse had seen them through the glass, pinned to the wall beside the stove. She had never seen a fox among them.\n\nOn the seventh night, the snow stopped, and the sky cleared into a sheet of stars. Ilse crept closer than she ever had. The window was fogged at the bottom, but she could see Maren's hand moving across the paper, pausing, moving again.\n\nThen the girl looked up.\n\nIlse froze, one paw lifted, her breath hanging white in the air. Maren's eyes went wide, and for a long moment neither of them moved.\n\nThen Maren smiled, slowly, and set down her pencil.\n\nThe next morning, Ilse found a small dish of cold chicken on the orchard wall, wrapped in a scrap of paper. On it, in careful pencil, was a drawing of a fox with its tail curled around its feet, looking very pleased with itself.\n\nIlse took the chicken. She left the drawing where it lay, because a fox has to be careful about what she carries home.\n\nBut that night, when the lamp glowed in the small window, she did not hide in the ditch. She sat in the open snow at the edge of the orchard, tail wrapped around her paws, and waited to be seen.\n\nMaren saw her, and laughed softly through the glass, and left the lamp burning.\n\nFrom then on, every winter, the girl left something on the wall: a bone, a crust of bread, a sketch of the moon. And every winter, the fox came down from the ridge to watch the lights, and to be watched in return."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21526,"cache_read_input_tokens":29474,"output_tokens":770,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":89},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":21526,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":770,"cache_read_input_tokens":29474,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21526,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":21526},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfrhDkLHBub4YTtTcPKBM","type":"assistant","uuid":"ba3ca22f-7235-42be-99b6-e6eaf0ae6622","timestamp":"2026-10-09T12:52:04.551Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"21836f70-90a0-4ca0-837b-2f1d58976556","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/private/tmp/hm-capture-claude","sessionId":"7d8ceea2-1c2b-4581-8f12-c261e4a673ec","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"master"}
